        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:118%">Note F of our formula rate tariff requires that the balances of 190, 281, 282 and 283 are to be adjusted by any amounts in contra accounts identified as regulatory assets or liabilities related to Financial Accounting Standards Board ("FASB") Accounting Standards Codification 740 - Income Taxes ("ASC 740") and exclude deferred income tax balances when the associated income tax consequences have been paid by others. Additionally, Note 2 in the Attachment O Formula Rate Template requires the exclusion of deferred taxes associated with the True-up Adjustment that are not otherwise included in rate base. Both the beginning balance and ending balance for Account 190 are Adjusted for ASC 740 and Other Items on Lines 20 and 24, respectively, of the section titled &#8220;Proration Used for True-up Revenue Requirement Calculation&#8221; in the ER20-13 Proration tab. These ASC 740 and Other Items include:</span>
      </div>
