    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">We have a net excess deferred income tax regulatory liability resulting from the implementation of the Federal Tax Cut and Jobs Act of 2017.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">We use RSGM for the amortization of (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes to customers. The deferred taxes associated with public utility plant property will be amortized over a period ranging from 3 to 70 years and deferred taxes not related to public utility property will be amortized over a period of 43 years.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">The total net (excess)/deficient income tax amortization of $(2,417,672), discussed further in the note shown on page 232, is used as the input to page 3, line 24a in our formula rate tariff.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">In accordance with the February 18, 2005 Order Approving Contested Settlement of the FERC in Docket Nos. ER04-691-002 and EL04-104-002 for FERC Electric Tariff Schedule 24 (110 FERC P61,177 2005), and with the August 5, 2005 Order in Docket Nos. ER04-691-045, EL04-104-043 and ER05-1083 for FERC Electric Tariff Schedule 24-A (112 FERC P61, 169 2005), the Balancing Authority costs included in FERC accounts 561.1 and 561.2 are $169,725 for the period January 1, 2025 through December 31, 2025.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Depreciation &amp; amortization of $2,226 is used for Accounts 351.1, 351.2, and 351.3 when the balance of Depreciation &amp; amortization is referenced (Attachment O, page 3, line 9) in Notes I and M of our Attachment GG and Attachment MM formula rate tariffs, respectively. Consistent with Order No. 898, METC revised its transmission formula rates to continue allocating transmission related computer hardware, software, and communication equipment costs to regionally cost shared projects, as accepted by FERC in Docket No. ER25 323.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
