    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-50" id="fn-50" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-51" id="fn-51" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rental amounts are assigned to ITC Affiliates based on a standardized methodology which identifies, records, and assigns costs related to shared assets and leased facilities to the affiliated business units benefiting from the usage of those shared assets. This standard methodology is generally considered an extension of ITC&#8217;s Direct Assignment Policy.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-52" id="fn-52" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rental Amounts are assigned to ITC Affiliates based on a standardized methodology which identifies, records, and assigns costs related to shared assets and leased facilities to the affiliated business units benefiting from the usage of those shared assets. This standard methodology is generally considered an extension of ITC's Direct Assignment Policy.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-53" id="fn-53" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amounts shown as transfers in column (f) from account 391 were solely for the purpose of implementing FERC Order 898 and represent transfers of computer hardware, software and communication equipment to newly established plant accounts 351.1, 351.2, 351.3, 397.1, 397.2, 397.3.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-54" id="fn-54" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The amount represents balances previously recorded to account 397 prior to implementation of FERC Order 898.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-55" id="fn-55" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This amount represents capitalized depreciation for vehicles and equipment used in the construction process.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-56" id="fn-56" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Net accumulated depreciation related to asset purchases and sales, and reserve adjustments persuant to a Commission approved depreciation study on docket #ER-22-4-000, December 1, 2021</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-57" id="fn-57" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The method for determination of depreciation rates shown in column (e) are straight line rates which when applied to monthly plant balances, will uniformly recover the unrecovered cost, adjusted for net salvage, over the remaining life of the plant.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-58" id="fn-58" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Average Remaining Life shown in column (g) is based on the latest approved depreciation study, which is based on balances as of December 31, 2020.&#160;</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-59" id="fn-59" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In addition to depreciation provided by application of reported rates, the 2025 provision for depreciation was reduced in the amount of $517,330 for certain general plant accounts, persuant to implementing the results of the 2021 depreciation study approved by the Commission on December 1, 2021, in docket #ER22-4-000</link:footnote>
