    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-66" id="fn-66" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Contains plant co-owned by International Transmission Company, which is an associated company.&#160; See Footnote 9, Jointly Owned Utility Plant / Coordinated Services on page 123.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-67" id="fn-67" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Member's Equity associated with the December 10, 2003 transaction referenced as the "2003 Equity Adjustment" on page 4, line number 25a of METC's Attachment O, was eliminated based on the September 21, 2006 FERC Order addressing disposition and acquisition of jurisdictional facilities in Docket No. EC06-123 and METC's April 10, 2007 accounting entry filing in Docket No. AC07-92.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-68" id="fn-68" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-69" id="fn-69" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with below the line operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-70" id="fn-70" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with below the line operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-71" id="fn-71" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All schedules use MISO as billing agent.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-72" id="fn-72" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Network load is populated on Schedule 9 on page 400. No information is provided in column (h) for billing demand, since these pages report Transmission Revenue dollars by schedule and demand information is not readily available (other than Schedule 9) and is maintained by MISO.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-73" id="fn-73" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">METC does not report &#8220;Number of Units&#8221; in columns (b), (c),(e) and (f): rather it only reports the total dollars. The quantity is not readily available and information pertaining to the amounts sold and purchased are maintained by MISO.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-74" id="fn-74" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">No information is reported in columns (e) &#8211; (j) as such information is maintained by MISO as the billing agent and not readily available. However, network load is reported in column (b).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-75" id="fn-75" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">METC is a transmission only company and as such, Monthly Energy and Sales for Resale information is not applicable.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-76" id="fn-76" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Senior Secured Notes listed were issued under our first mortgage indenture and secured by a first mortgage lien on substantially all of our property.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-77" id="fn-77" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">During the year ended December 31, 2025, we borrowed $482,500,000 and repaid $374,400,000 under the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-78" id="fn-78" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents borrowings under intercompany loan agreement of $50,000,000 and borrowings under the revolving credit agreement of $482,500,000</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-79" id="fn-79" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents issuance of long-term debt of $85,000,000 and borrowings under the revolving credit agreement of $302,100,000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-80" id="fn-80" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-81" id="fn-81" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-82" id="fn-82" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents cash balance in accounts 131 and 136.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-83" id="fn-83" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents cash balance in accounts 131 and 136.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-84" id="fn-84" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The study included on this page is a generator interconnection study.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-85" id="fn-85" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor non-plant timing differences primarily associated with tax gross-up on state deficient deferred income tax regulatory asset.</link:footnote>
